    "summary": "For the derivative of the composition of functions like f ( x ) = sin( x ), we can not use the product rule. The functions don’t hold hands like in a product, they are “chained” in the sense that we evaluate first x then apply the sin function to it. In order to differentiate, take the derivative of the x then multiply this with the derivative of the function sin evaluated at x . The answer is cos( x )7 x . Here is the rule:",
